course: dictionary
lesson: 4229
title: Words about grammar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Grammar is the set of rules for how words fit together in a language. «Grammatical» is the word we use when those rules are followed. «Is this sentence grammatical?» asks: do the words follow the rules?
explain: A grammatical mistake breaks a rule. «They was happy at the party» is not grammatical, because «they» needs «were». Teachers mark grammatical mistakes in writing so you can fix them.
explain: Two meanings can be in one word. In «Is this sentence grammatical?» it means correct by the rules. In «a grammatical mistake» it means to do with grammar. Read the words around it to see which one fits.
explain: Grammar rules change from language to language. «Ukrainian nouns have grammatical gender, a grammar label, not boy or girl.» So in Ukrainian, «стіл» (table) is masculine, «книга» (book) is feminine, and «вікно» (window) is neuter. Here «grammatical» means to do with grammar.
fact: Grammar is the set of rules for how words are put together in a language.
fact: «Grammatical» means correct according to the rules of grammar.
fact: «Grammatical» can also mean to do with grammar, as in «a grammatical mistake».
fact: «They was happy» is not grammatical, because «they» goes with «were».
fact: Ukrainian nouns have grammatical gender: «стіл» (table) is masculine, «книга» (book) is feminine, «вікно» (window) is neuter.
exercise: Which sentence is grammatical? | They was happy at the party. | *They were happy at the party. | Party the happy were they.
exercise: «The teacher circled a grammatical mistake in my story.» What does grammatical mean here? | Written in pencil | Very long | Funny | *To do with grammar
exercise: In Ukrainian, «стіл» (table) is masculine. What is the grammar label in this example? | Gender | Colour | *Gender, masculine | Size
test: Mrs Patel asks, «Is this sentence grammatical?» What is she asking? | Whether the sentence is true | Whether the sentence is written neatly | Whether the sentence is long | *Whether the sentence follows the rules of grammar
test: Ella says, «My sentence was marked for grammatical mistakes.» What were the marks for? | Missing pages | Drawings in the margin | Handwriting that is too big | *Breaking the rules of grammar
exam: Which word means correct according to the rules of grammar? | *Grammatical | Sentence | Grammar | Rule
